.nh
.TH "PB-RECIPE-UPDATE" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-recipe-update - Change a recipe from its file


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb recipe update -f <file> [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Change a recipe to what its file now says; the recipe is named by the file's base
name. The token stays the same. Online machines from the recipe apply the new
revision at once (tags change server-side; ENV, config, preview and tunnel sections
are created, changed or removed on each machine).

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-f\fP, \fB--file\fP=""
	the recipe file (.toml or .json)

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for update

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print JSON


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  pb recipe update -f ci.toml
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-recipe(1)\fP
